---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getProjects } from '../lib/content';
const projects = await getProjects();
---

<Base
  title="About"
  current="/about"
  description="Travis Dater is a systems administrator who builds practical Android tools for car head units, TVs and troubleshooting."
>
  <div class="wrap about section">
    <div class="about__intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Hi, I'm Travis.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm a systems administrator. My day job is making other people's technology behave, and my
        evenings, apparently, are for making my own technology behave too.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="about__grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Why I build these</h2>
        <p>
          Systems administration teaches you to notice the same failure twice and to automate it
          away the third time. These projects come from that habit. A head unit with a useless stock
          launcher, a TV that can't drive a web page, and troubleshooting notes spread across six
          apps are all problems I'd rather fix than keep tolerating.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm not a software company. There's no team, no support desk and no release schedule. It's
          one person building tools for real problems and sharing them as-is. What I can offer is
          honesty about what each one does, what it doesn't, and how finished it is.
        </p>

        <h2>What I'm into</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Android apps</strong>, especially ones that run somewhere other than a phone,
            like a dashboard or a TV.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Automotive diagnostics and telemetry</strong>: OBD-II, live sensor data, and
            making cheap adapters useful.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Bluetooth and BLE</strong>, and the special kind of joy that is debugging them
            on a head unit.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Vehicle electronics</strong> and hands-on installs.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI integrations</strong> that stay honest about what they know, which is why
            BLACKBOX keeps AI suggestions separate from evidence.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Practical troubleshooting</strong>: evidence first, one variable at a time, and
            "unknown" is an acceptable answer.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <p>
          Ship something small that works, test it on real hardware, fix what breaks, and write down
          why. You can see that in the decision trail on each project page. Each step links to the
          release or document it came from, so none of it is a reconstructed origin myth.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it's heading</h2>
        <p>
          These are directions, not promises. BLACKBOX's roadmap points toward physical project work
          like component labels, installation history and instrument readings, and then toward
          controlled experiments. KITT Launcher keeps getting refined on real head units. Anything
          new shows up on this site when there's a real release to download, not before.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about__aside">
        <div class="panel panel--accent">
          <h2 class="h3">The projects</h2>
          <ul class="about__list">
            {projects.map((p) => (
              <li style={`--accent:${p.accent}`}>
                <a href={`/projects/${p.slug}`}>{p.title}</a>
                <span class="hint">{p.tagline}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h2 class="h3">Get in touch</h2>
          <p>
            The <a href="/feedback">feedback form</a> is the way to reach me about the projects. I
            don't publish personal contact details, and I don't do support contracts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about__intro {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }
  .about__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.6fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-7);
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .about__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .about__aside {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-content: start;
  }
  .h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .about__list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .about__list li {
    display: grid;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
  }
  .about__list a {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
</style>
